  "id": "cumulative-rehearsal",
  "term": "cumulative rehearsal",
  "definition": "Cumulative rehearsal is a memory-maintenance strategy in which a person repeatedly rehearses material to help keep it active in working memory. In the supplied study, training in this strategy improved recall during a distracting delay, suggesting it supports remembering by encouraging rehearsal.",
